WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.320
Hi, I'm Gabe Alain Huppe,
founder of avoiddivorce.com.

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:07.540
We provide divorce avoidance and
relationship coaching services for men who

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:08.820
are currently in marital crisis.

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:11.040
If you're one of these men,
there are a few things you should know.

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:12.200
First of all, you're not alone.

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:15.700
A lot of men find themselves in this
situation and some of them are eventually

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:17.200
able to find a way out.

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:20.800
Second, you likely have a lot more
influence over your situation than you

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:21.600
think you have.

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:24.820
Even if your partner has emotionally
checked out or said she's done,

00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:28.760
there are a number of things you can do to
try to bring your relationship back on the

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:29.100
right path.

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:31.760
And third, there's a new option for you.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:34.900
One-on-one coaching can help
you address your marital issues.

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:40.860
You don't have to drag yourself and your
partner to couples counselling or rely

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:46.120
on the advice of family and friends or go
about this process entirely on your own.

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:49.360
So what is it that we
provide at avoiddivorce.com?

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:53.840
I've assembled a team of coaches to
essentially take you through three stages.

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:56.140
In the first stage,
which we call stabilization,

00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:59.000
the goal is to get you back
to your own personal baseline.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:01.620
If you've struggled in your
marriage for some time,

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:03.980
chances are you're probably stressed out,

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:06.680
overwhelmed and unsure
about what to do next.

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:09.660
You've probably also neglected your
own goals for a period of time.

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:14.460
We want to get you back on your feet so
that you can think clearly and act with

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:15.500
greater intention.

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:18.260
And that's going to help you in
your relationship, but frankly,

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:21.000
it's going to help you in a lot
of different areas in your life.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:25.680
Now, while we're doing that, we also want
you to start gaining an appreciation and

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:30.440
understanding for the harmful patterns in
your relationship and your role in those

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:31.020
patterns.

00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:36.100
And we want you to start trying to stop
doing those things that are hurting

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:37.380
yourself and your partner.

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:41.240
Now, we don't expect major changes
overnight during the stabilization phase,

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:47.060
but we do want to see what the roadblocks
are and to better understand the things

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:48.580
that we need to overcome together.

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:51.500
Now, once you've stabilized
yourself and the relationship,

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:53.140
we then move on to the repair phase.

00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:56.400
During the repair phase,
you learn new skills in communication,

00:01:56.680 --> 00:01:59.620
emotional regulation and
relational leadership.

00:01:59.660 --> 00:02:02.900
And we'll start rebuilding different
aspects that have been lost through the

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:03.460
years.

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:07.000
This includes your partner's emotional
safety, their sense of connection,

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:11.220
their sense of attraction and respect, the
mutual admiration you have for each other.

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:15.860
We want to go step by step and find
different opportunities to rebuild.

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:19.760
Now, once we sufficiently rebuild, we move
on to the next stage, which is re-commit.

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:24.000
During the re-commit phase, the ideal
scenario is that the two of you start

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:28.680
feeling excited about the future together
again and truly want to re-commit your

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:29.920
lives to each other.

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:34.060
Now, I should say that none of
these stages are a quick fix.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:38.360
Your partner is going to want to see
sustained evidence of change from you over

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:39.860
a long period of time.

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:43.360
Second, there is no guarantee about
how your partner is going to respond.

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:45.000
You can't control her choices.

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:48.260
She might decide to re-commit with
you or she might decide to move on.

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:52.200
The right approach to this coaching
program is for you to decide to work on

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:54.440
yourself irrespective of the outcome.

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:58.220
And if that's your mindset, then the good
thing is that you're going to be very

00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:03.040
long-term oriented and you're not going
to be so affected by how your partner

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:04.400
responds on the day-to-day.

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:07.980
And that's going to help you with
recovering your marriage and just

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:10.740
recovering yourself really
and improving yourself.

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:14.080
Now, if this is something that
sounds interesting to you,

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:16.760
you think you might want
to enroll in this program,

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:19.160
why not book a free
discovery call with me?

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:20.500
We'll go over your questions.

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:24.280
I'll discuss the different details of our
program and we'll find out if this program

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:25.820
is the right next step for you.

00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:27.060
Hope to talk to you soon.
